[TITLE]
OTHER 110 (deterministic): pure pipes, every link OPEN, no valves anywhere.
BIG pipe J1-J2 has near-zero head-loss gradient, so pipecoeff() caps its
gradient at RQtol/Hexp. RQTOL is set to 1.852*2^-24 so the capped gradient
is exactly 2^-24 and the pipe conductance exactly 2^24. The hair-thin feed
pipes contribute ~1e-20, which vanishes when added to 2^24 in doubles.
Cholesky: sqrt(2^24)=2^12 and (2^24/2^12)^2=2^24 are all exact, so the
second pivot is exactly 0.0 -> linsolve returns the node -> no control
valve to blame -> Error 110 at trial 1. Failing node is reachable from
both reservoirs through OPEN pipes and touches no valve of any kind.

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID    Elev   Demand
 J1    0      1
 J2    0      0

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID    Head
 R1    100
 R2    50

[PIPES]
;ID     Node1  Node2  Length    Diam    Roughness  MinorLoss  Status
 HAIR1  R1     J1     1000000   0.001   1          0          OPEN
 BIG    J1     J2     0.1       10000   1000000    0          OPEN
 HAIR2  J2     R2     1000000   0.001   1          0          OPEN

[REPORT]
 STATUS    FULL
 MESSAGES  YES
 SUMMARY   YES

[OPTIONS]
 UNITS     GPM
 HEADLOSS  H-W
 TRIALS    200
 ACCURACY  0.001
 RQTOL     1.1038780212402344e-07

[TIMES]
 DURATION  0

[END]
